      "description": "Aoshima is a small subtropical island connected to the mainland by a bridge, famous for the 'Devil's Washboard' — a natural formation of parallel basalt rock ridges extending along the shore, created by ancient wave erosion. The island's center houses Aoshima Shrine, a colorful shrine surrounded by lush tropical vegetation.",
